In PHP, `new C()` creates an instance of class C. Then `->hi()` calls the method `hi()` on that instance, which returns the string 'hi'. Then `echo` prints it.

In PHP 8.0+, `new C()` is automatically parenthesized, so `new C()->hi()` is valid and equivalent to `(new C())->hi()`. This has been the case since PHP 8.0. In PHP 8.5, this would still work the same way.

The output is the string `hi`.

